#scene("standard_ui")

@bg("classroom")
@startBgm("main_theme")

The classroom is quiet before the club meeting begins.

@show("alice_smile", position="center")

:: Alice
This screen uses @tsuzuru/standard-ui-preact for message and choice UI.

@voice("alice_001")

:: Alice
Visual and audio state are still connected by example-local layers.

@show("bob_normal", position="left")
@se("click")

:: Bob
The package stays focused on standard UI components.

? What should Alice do next?
- "Greet Bob" -> #greet_bob
- "Check the room" -> #check_room

#label("greet_bob")

:: Alice
Good afternoon, Bob.

@jump("#after_choice")

#label("check_room")

The room has no bundled images yet, so missing assets are shown as fallback boxes.

@jump("#after_choice")

#label("after_choice")

@hide("alice_smile")

Alice steps away from the center of the room.

@waitClick()

@show("alice_smile", position="right")

:: Alice
Click, Enter, or Space can advance standard message windows.

@page()

@hide("bob_normal")
@stopBgm()

The example reaches the end safely even without bundled media files.
